            <ArticleTitle>Forefoot complaints--the Morton's metatarsalgia. The role of MR imaging.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>221-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An illustrated case with Morton's metatarsalgia is presented. MR imaging was helpful for determining the presence, location and magnitude of intermetatarsal neuroma. Moreover, it had a large influence on the differential diagnostic thinking because many disorders may produce forefoot complaints mimicking Morton's metatarsalgia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
